          "@value": "dak-l1-library"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Build a DAK's library from the L1 sources its Component 1 cites, and the L1 knowledge graph that records them. Read when starting or extending a DAK library, when a DAK's guidance changes, and before writing any L1 graph for a DAK. Covers fetching a cited WHO IRIS item, ingesting it, deciding whether it is L1 (declared > context > inferred), extracting the Component 1 graph, the L1 graph of each L1 source as a specialisation of its library entry, and the layering rule: the library is upstream of L1."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "dak-l1-library",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/skills/content/authoring-who-smart-guidelines/dak-l1-library.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
